    ('ARCH425', 'History of Architecture I', 3, 3, 'Pre-1500 World Architecture survey course - History of Architecture structured to develop critical thinking and visually literacy with regard to the worldwide legacy of design thinking and cultural production through architecture. Structured to nurture critical thinking and visually literacy with regard to the worldwide legacy of architecture. The work in the course will involve the evaluation of sources and arguments in reading architectural history. Architecture will be framed relative to ways of thinking, religious beliefs, cultural heritage, and cultural values.', NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Permission of ARCH-Architecture Program.', 'ARCH225 or ARCH425.', '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/arch/', 'none', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Graduate architecture history course requires additional recitation section and additional coursework tied to survey lectures.'),
