    ('COMX102', 'Introduction to Visual Culture', 3, 3, 'Utilizes theory to understand the role of visual culture within daily lives, exploring a range of media from renaissance painting to TV, magazines, internet media, gaming and infographics. Explores visual media analysis; the evolution of visual codes; the impact of changing technologies; media literacy; information graphics literacy; meme and viral culture.', NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/comx/', 'none', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This course is offered as part of the Maryland-in-Rome study abroad program. Students must apply for this program through Education Abroad: More information at ter.ps/UMRome. Education Abroad processes registrations for this course on behalf of students.'),
    ('COMX103', 'Communication and Society', 3, 3, 'Explores the relationship between communications, media, society, and culture. Within historical and contemporary contexts, the subject addresses how audiences and participants negotiate media in their lives. Focuses on different media forms, from newspapers to television, and from books to mobile technology. Topics covered include the effects of media on audiences; issues of race and gender in the media; media ownership and regulation; the impact of technological development and institutional pressures on media uses, content, and patterns of communication. Assesses ethical and legal issues which media users and practitioners may face.', NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/comx/', 'none', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This course is offered as part of the Maryland-in-Rome study abroad program. Students must apply for this program through Education Abroad: More information at ter.ps/UMRome. Education Abroad processes registrations for this course on behalf of students.'),
    ('COMX201', 'Social Media: an Italian Perspective', 3, 3, 'The world of social media has its own specialized vocabulary. Key terms such as "social media strategy", "followers", "engagement" and "content marketing" will form the basis of our study. Nowadays, thanks to the internet, the small market downtown has enlarged its boundaries worldwide and mere shouting louder has been replaced by advertising through social media. Hence, the title of this course: Social media, yes, but from an Italian perspective.', NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/comx/', 'none', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This course is offered as part of the Maryland-in-Florence study abroad program. Students must apply for this program through Education Abroad: More information at ter.ps/UMFlorence. Education Abroad processes registrations for this course on behalf of students.'),
    ('COMX300', 'Media and Gender', 3, 3, 'Media representations of men and women influence and affect interpretations of sexual identities, interpretations of social roles, and perceptions of equality or inequality in society. This course reviews the extent and importance of media influences through a study of representations of men and women and alternative sexualities in the popular media and advertising in the latter half of the 20th century.', NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/comx/', 'none', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This course is offered as part of the Maryland-in-Rome study abroad program. Students must apply for this program through Education Abroad: More information at ter.ps/UMRome. Education Abroad processes registrations for this course on behalf of students.'),
    ('COMX311', 'Social Media, Social Food', 3, 3, 'What is "Social Media" and how will developing media skills help students plan successful careers in the world of food? This course will provide a perfect example of the importance of communication and social media in the food industry.', NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, 'COMX200 or COMX311.', '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/comx/', 'none', 'none_found', NULL, 'COMX200.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This course is offered as part of the Maryland-in-Florence study abroad program. Students must apply for this program through Education Abroad: More information at ter.ps/UMFlorence. Education Abroad processes registrations for this course on behalf of students.'),
    ('COMX312', 'Media and Globalization', 3, 3, 'Provides students with critical perspectives on contemporary globalized media - where media are analyzed as industries, technological devices and transnational cultural flows. Adopts a comparative and historical perspective in the approach to the analysis of media and globalization. Explores how key areas history, industrialization, economics, and culture interact with contemporary international communication systems.', NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/comx/', 'none', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This course is offered as part of the Maryland-in-Rome study abroad program. Students must apply for this program through Education Abroad: More information at ter.ps/UMRome. Education Abroad processes registrations for this course on behalf of students.'),
    ('COMX315', 'Strategic Communication', 3, 3, 'Explores strategic communication in an increasingly complex world. Through theoretical perspectives, case studies, and a hands-on project develops a deeper understanding of the strategic framework that underlies efficient and meaningful communications. Includes two study tours which will allow engagement in various topics related to organizational, strategic, and personal communication and to meet professionals in the field.', NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, NULL, 'N/A.', '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/comx/', 'none', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'This course is offered as part of the Maryland-in-Copenhagen study abroad program. Students must apply for this program through Education Abroad: More information at ter.ps/UMCopenhagen. Education Abroad processes registrations for this course on behalf of students.'),
    ('CPBE100', 'College Park Scholars: Business, Society & Entrepreneurship First-Year Colloquium', 1, 1, 'Introductory colloquium: Examination of issues related to business, society and entrepreneurship.', NULL, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Students must be matriculated into the College Park Scholars Business, Society & Entrepreneurship (CPBE) program.', NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/cpbe/', 'none', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
    ('CPBE101', 'College Park Scholars: Business, Society and Entrepreneurship First-Year Colloquium II', 1, 1, 'The course is the second of three colloquia for the BSE Scholars program scheduled for their second semester (Spring). This colloquium is designed to emphasize the entrepreneurial focus of the BSE program by giving students the opportunity for practical, real-life and personal exposure to entrepreneurial activities.', 'CPBE100.', NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Students must be matriculated into the College Park Scholars Business, Society & Entrepreneurship program.', NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/cpbe/', 'parsed', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
    ('CPBE200', 'College Park Scholars: Business, Society and Entrepreneurship: Second-Year Colloquium I', 1, 1, 'The third of three colloquia for the BSE Scholars program is designed to expose and engage students in real-life and real-time entrepreneurial challenges. BSE partners with two organizations that bring current and relevant challenges to the class. Students work in small teams to explore a highly experiential start-up challenge.', 'CPBE101.', NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Must be enrolled in the College Park Scholars Business, Society, & Entrepreneurship (CPBE) program.', 'CPSP218B or CPBE200.', '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/cpbe/', 'parsed', 'none_found', NULL, 'CPSP218B.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
    ('CPBE225', 'Enterprise Communications', 3, 3, 'Examines basic interpersonal communication processes within written and oral channels, with practical applications for the business environment.', 'CPBE100.', NULL, TRUE, 'FSOC', 'Must be enrolled in College Park Scholars'' Business, Society and Entrepreneurship (CPBE) program.', NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/cpbe/', 'parsed', 'verified', '202608', 'CPSP220.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
    ('CPBE230', 'College Park Scholars: Business, Society & Entrepreneurship Internship Practicum', 1, 3, 'Supervised internship project in an area related to business, society and entrepreneurship.', 'CPBE100.', NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Students must be matriculated into the College Park Scholars Business, Society & entrepreneurship (CPBE) program.', NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/cpbe/', 'parsed', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
    ('CPBE240', 'College Park Scholars: Business, Society & Entrepreneurship Service-Learning Practicum', 1, 3, 'Supervised Service-Learning project in an area related to business, society and entrepreneurship.', 'CPBE100.', NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Students must be matriculated into the College Park Scholars Business, Society & Entrepreneurship (CPBE) program.', NULL, '2026-2027', 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/approved-courses/cpbe/', 'parsed', 'none_found', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
